  "id": "COMPOUND:14504 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Metronidazole is implicated in the targeting of Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that metronidazole acts as a target for Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8, which in turn is targeted by compounds such as 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and Phorone, both of which are themselves targets of SDR family member 9. This indicates a chain of interactions where metronidazole indirectly influences the SDR family member 9 through these intermediates. The presence of multiple pathways converging on SDR family member 9 suggests a potential mechanism involving enzyme inhibition or modulation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the metabolic and enzymatic processes involved, emphasizing the role of SDR family member 9 in mediating the effects of metronidazole.",
